// schedule.js — hand-authored weekly workout configuration.
//
// This is the ONLY place you need to edit to change which exercises happen
// on which day. It maps each weekday to a workout name + an ordered list of
// exercise ids (ids come from js/data/exercises.js, generated by
// tools/generate_exercise_data.py).
//
// HOW TO ADD A NEW EXERCISE TO A DAY:
//   1. Make sure the exercise folder + EXERCISE_META entry exist, then run
//      `python tools/generate_exercise_data.py` to regenerate exercises.js.
//   2. Add its id string to the `exerciseIds` array of the day you want it
//      to appear on (order in the array = order shown during the workout).
//
// HOW TO MARK A DAY AS REST:
//   Set `rest: true` and leave `exerciseIds` empty (see "sun" below).
//
// Day keys use JS's Date.getDay() convention: 0=Sunday ... 6=Saturday.

